{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 100, "previous": "/api/v1/doc/document/?format=json&name__startswith=draft-ietf-tls&limit=100&offset=0", "total_count": 113}, "objects": [{"abstract": "The United States Government has published guidelines for \"NSA Suite\r\n   B Cryptography\" dated July, 2005, which defines cryptographic\r\n   algorithm polcy for national security applications.  This document\r\n   defines a profile of TLS which is conformant with Suite B.", "ad": null, "expires": "2007-10-25T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 34164, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-suiteb", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-suiteb/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/6/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2007-05-03T07:00:00Z", "title": "Suite B Cipher Suites for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 1888}, {"abstract": "   TLS 1.3 records limit the inner plaintext (TLSInnerPlaintext) size to\n   2^14 + 1 bytes, which includes one byte for the content type.  DTLS\n   1.3 uses the same plaintext size limit.  This document defines a TLS\n   extension that allows endpoints to advertise larger per-direction\n   maximum inner plaintext sizes, up to 2^30 - 256 bytes, while reducing\n   overhead in TLS 1.3 and DTLS 1.3 record headers.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2026-10-09T07:57:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 141707, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-super-jumbo-record-limit/", "rev": "03", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/42/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/147470/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152373/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157224/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161959/"], "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/rev-wglc/"], "time": "2026-10-09T07:09:04Z", "title": "Large Record Sizes for TLS and DTLS with Reduced Overhead", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   To use TLS Encrypted ClientHello (ECH) the client needs to learn the\n   ECH configuration for a server before it attempts a connection to the\n   server.  This specification provides a mechanism for conveying the\n   ECH configuration information via DNS, using a SVCB or HTTPS resource\n   record (RR).\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2025-12-18T14:02:41Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 120863, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-svcb-ech", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 10, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-svcb-ech/", "rev": "08", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/145370/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/144556/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/136893/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141578/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/142708/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145075/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/147011/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/149147/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152781/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-03-04T05:51:52Z", "title": "Bootstrapping TLS Encrypted ClientHello with DNS Service Bindings", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "TLS session tickets enable stateless connection resumption for clients without server-side, per-client state.  Servers vend an arbitrary number of session tickets to clients, at their discretion, upon connection establishment.  Clients store and use tickets when resuming future connections.  This document describes a mechanism by which clients can specify the desired number of tickets needed for future connections.  This extension aims to provide a means for servers to determine the number of tickets to generate in order to reduce ticket waste while simultaneously priming clients for future connection attempts.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2021-06-07T02:20:22Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 89077, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 8, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-ticketrequests/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/100854/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/104139/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/106754/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/107123/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/107877/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/111662/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/116165/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/115976/"], "tags": [], "time": "2022-04-25T23:44:28Z", "title": "TLS Ticket Requests", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Use of TLS 1.3, which fixes some known deficiencies in TLS 1.2, is\n   growing.  This document specifies that outside of urgent security\n   fixes (as determine by TLS WG consensus), new TLS Exporter Labels, or\n   new Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation (ALPN) Protocol IDs, no\n   changes will be approved for TLS 1.2.  This prescription does not\n   pertain to DTLS (in any DTLS version); it pertains to TLS only.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2025-10-05T14:36:38Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 135463, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tls12-frozen", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 6, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tls12-frozen/", "rev": "08", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/150808/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141728/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/144633/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/148129/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145087/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/147916/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/148117/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/148801/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150987/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-07-15T23:40:23Z", "title": "TLS 1.2 is in Feature Freeze", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document specifies version 1.3 of the Transport Layer Security (TLS) protocol. TLS allows client/server applications to communicate over the Internet in a way that is designed to prevent eavesdropping, tampering, and message forgery.\n\n This document updates RFCs 5705 and 6066, and obsoletes RFCs 5077, 5246, and 6961. This document also specifies new requirements for TLS 1.2 implementations.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/104851/", "expires": "2018-09-21T21:26:15Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 55251, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tls13", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 160, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tls13/", "rev": "28", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/ps/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/59397/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/59398/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/61729/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/64520/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/65644/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/67695/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/70123/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/70989/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/71776/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/72481/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/73392/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/74860/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/77260/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/78266/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/79977/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/80556/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/81099/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/81687/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/81857/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/84956/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/86252/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92891/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/88268/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91422/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/92066/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93465/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/93544/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/94182/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/94319/"], "tags": [], "time": "2020-03-07T08:26:41Z", "title": "The Transport Layer Security (TLS) Protocol Version 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 35738}, {"abstract": "This document specifies a TLS 1.3 extension that allows a server to authenticate with a combination of a certificate and an external pre-shared key (PSK).", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2020-06-25T13:50:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 88807, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/exp/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tls13-cert-with-extern-psk", "note": "", "notify": "Joseph Salowey <joe@salowey.net>", "pages": 11, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-cert-with-extern-psk/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/joe@salowey.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/154/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/exp/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/101649/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/103657/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/104025/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108223/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108768/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108800/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108812/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/108813/"], "tags": [], "time": "2023-08-12T07:16:30Z", "title": "TLS 1.3 Extension for Certificate-Based Authentication with an External Pre-Shared Key", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document allocates code points for the use of RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5\n   with client certificates in TLS 1.3.  This removes an obstacle for\n   some deployments to migrate to TLS 1.3.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/112723/", "expires": "2026-06-05T20:03:12Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 123331, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tls13-pkcs1", "note": "", "notify": "sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 7, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-pkcs1/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/151981/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/147572/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/138667/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/142714/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155313/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155532/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155931/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157900/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-04-28T23:29:58Z", "title": "Legacy RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5 codepoints for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document includes examples of TLS 1.3 handshakes.  Private keys and inputs are provided so that these handshakes might be reproduced.  Intermediate values, including secrets, traffic keys, and IVs, are shown so that implementations might be checked incrementally against these values.", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/115214/", "expires": "2019-03-31T18:08:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75116, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/inf/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tls13-vectors", "note": "", "notify": "Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>", "pages": 68, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tls13-vectors/", "rev": "07", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/3/", "/api/v1/doc/state/110/", "/api/v1/doc/state/113/", "/api/v1/doc/state/7/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": "/api/v1/name/stdlevelname/inf/", "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/83550/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/87713/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/88312/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/91531/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/95084/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/95529/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/96937/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/98298/"], "tags": [], "time": "2019-02-28T11:05:42Z", "title": "Example Handshake Traces for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 5591}, {"abstract": "   A number of extensions are proposed in the TLS working group that\n   carry no interesting information except the 1-bit indication that a\n   certain optional feature is supported.  Such extensions take 4 octets\n   each.  This document defines a flags extension that can provide such\n   indications at an average marginal cost of 1 bit each.  More\n   precisely, it provides as many flag extensions as needed at 4 + the\n   order of the last set bit divided by 8.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-03-15T04:01:02Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 92688, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags", "note": "", "notify": "Christopher Wood <caw@heapingbits.net>, sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags/", "rev": "18", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/105974/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/107990/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/110072/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/112917/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/117067/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/119115/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/120555/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/122430/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/123495/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/125106/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/168880/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/127793/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/131237/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/135566/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/141283/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145602/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150463/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155275/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161228/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-09-11T04:01:02Z", "title": "A Flags Extension for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   This document defines the TLS Trust Anchors extension, a mechanism\n   for a TLS client or server to select a certificate to present based\n   on the peer's trusted certification authorities.  It describes\n   certification authorities more succinctly than the TLS Certificate\n   Authorities extension.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2027-04-03T15:10:48Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 143262, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 41, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/", "rev": "06", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/149501/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/152064/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/155314/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/161382/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/162794/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/169727/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/169043/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-09-30T15:10:48Z", "title": "TLS Trust Anchor Identifiers", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "This document suggests extensions to TLS designed to make TLS more \r\namenable to use within wireless environments. The extensions may be\r\nused by TLS clients and servers. The extensions are backwards\r\ncompatible - communication is possible between TLS 1.0 clients\r\nthat support the extensions and TLS 1.0 servers that do not\r\nsupport the extensions, and vice versa.\r\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2001-05-25T07:00:00Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 23491, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wireless", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 13, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wireless/", "rev": "00", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/38/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": [], "tags": [], "time": "2000-11-27T08:00:00Z", "title": "Wireless Extensions to TLS\r\n", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": 3482}, {"abstract": "   We define a well-known URI at which an HTTP origin can inform an\n   authoritative DNS server, or other interested parties, about its\n   Service Bindings.  Service binding data can include Encrypted\n   ClientHello (ECH) configurations, that may change frequently.  This\n   allows the HTTP origin, in collaboration with DNS infrastructure\n   elements, to publish and rotate its own ECH keys.  Other service\n   binding data such as information about TLS supported groups is\n   unlikely to change quickly, but the HTTP origin is much more likely\n   to have accurate information when changes do occur.  Service data\n   published via this mechanism is typically available via an HTTPS or\n   SVCB resource record.\n", "ad": null, "expires": "2026-11-04T13:14:44Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 109386, "intended_std_level": null, "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-wkech", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 21, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-wkech/", "rev": "12", "rfc": null, "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": null, "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "submissions": ["/api/v1/submit/submission/143952/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/127685/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/129494/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/133357/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/134716/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/137697/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/145956/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/150985/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/153719/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/154988/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/156451/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/157247/", "/api/v1/submit/submission/162841/"], "tags": [], "time": "2026-05-03T13:14:44Z", "title": "A well-known URI for publishing service parameters", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}]}